[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4860485356","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120841#issuecomment-4860485356","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120841","id":4860485356,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIbUe7A","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-01T22:18:56Z","updated_at":"2026-07-01T22:39:50Z","body":"I assume the essence of this request is to synchronize animations of different durations. Then, is there a reason or use case that justifies the need for a curve here? Why wouldn’t a single boolean option like `adjust_length_by_speed_scale` with xfade suffice? We should not implement options that overlap with the functionality of xfade.\r\n\r\nAlso, as pointed out in similar implementation in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117275, since we cannot guarantee that the duration of animations other than NodeAnimation won’t change midway through, even if we were to implement `adjust_length_by_speed_scale` as an option, we would need to restrict it to connections between NodeAnimations only, by the similar way with https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117275.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4860485356/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4860603582","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120841#issuecomment-4860603582","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120841","id":4860603582,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIbbsvg","user":{"login":"low-moon","id":298359369,"node_id":"U_kgDOEciaSQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/298359369?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon","html_url":"https://github.com/low-moon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-01T22:40:48Z","updated_at":"2026-07-01T22:45:00Z","body":"It is intended to give more control over how the current position is transferred during a sync transition. The main use case that inspired this change is the need to invert the sync position so that the next state can perform the inverse of the current state after the sync, but I chose to implement it as a curve to allow for more control over other situations where the usual sync is restricting, such as if the two animations are different lengths. \r\n\r\nIt essentially acts as a remap of the current playback position to the new playback position at the instant of the sync, so I don't think it overlaps with xfade or custom_timeline, unless I am misunderstanding that functionality. I imagine most uses of this curve would be linear, as the intended use of the curve is to set the min_from, max_from, min_to and max_to of the hypothetical remap.\r\n\r\nI understand the duration can change for non-animation states, but the sync position is only calculated at the instant the transition is triggered, so the length changing as a result shouldn't affect the position that is chosen.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4860603582/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4860771889","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120841#issuecomment-4860771889","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120841","id":4860771889,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIbl-MQ","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-01T23:13:39Z","updated_at":"2026-07-01T23:32:52Z","body":"I see, now I understand that it doesn’t conflict with xfade. However, I’m still skeptical about whether it really needs to be a curve.\r\n\r\n> I imagine most uses of this curve would be linea\r\n\r\nYes, I think so too.\r\n\r\nI assume the lack of documentation is one reason, curve is not intuitive. So if your intention is to allow remapping of `from_start`/`from_end` and `to_start`/`to_end`, I think it would be more intuitive to simply use those values as property names.\r\n\r\nIn this case, I think using \"seconds\" as the unit would be more intuitive, but in cases other than NodeAnimation, this would create a problem where settings cannot be shared across animations of different lengths. Therefore, the implementation would need to either restrict this option to NodeAnimation only or allow users to switch between \"seconds/cycles\" units.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4860771889/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4860920987","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120841#issuecomment-4860920987","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120841","id":4860920987,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIbvEmw","user":{"login":"low-moon","id":298359369,"node_id":"U_kgDOEciaSQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/298359369?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon","html_url":"https://github.com/low-moon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-01T23:43:31Z","updated_at":"2026-07-01T23:43:31Z","body":"As an argument for using the curve, if one of the animations has a different rate to the other or goes through stages of recovery, the curve allows precise mapping of if the first animation has only played slightly it can be recovered quickly, and past a point it then jumps to a position in the second animation that takes longer to recover. This can probably be configured without the curve using code, but the curve allows easier configuration of more complex transitions.\r\n\r\nI am unsure about using seconds as like you say it restricts the configuration to be specifically about two animations, but the alpha based units are not as easy to convert from the animation. Maybe the documentation could explicitly state that it is operating in units relative to the animation lengths, and an example on how to convert from a time in the animation to the correct alpha by dividing it by the length?\r\n\r\nIf this general remapping is too unintuitive or niche to be added, it could just be replaced by a boolean to invert the sync position? As this is the more in-demand use-case and is something that I have found is missing for certain uses of the animation system and is difficult to work around.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4860920987/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5073479833","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120841#issuecomment-5073479833","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120841","id":5073479833,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLmcomQ","user":{"login":"shanayyy","id":13399488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMzk5NDg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13399488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanayyy","html_url":"https://github.com/shanayyy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanayyy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanayyy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanayyy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanayyy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanayyy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanayyy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanayyy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanayyy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanayyy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-24T19:02:22Z","updated_at":"2026-07-24T19:02:22Z","body":"Can the blend2 node be used in a similar way to synchronize the foot phase of walking and running?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5073479833/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5074221942","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120841#issuecomment-5074221942","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120841","id":5074221942,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLnJ7dg","user":{"login":"low-moon","id":298359369,"node_id":"U_kgDOEciaSQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/298359369?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon","html_url":"https://github.com/low-moon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/low-moon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-24T20:44:27Z","updated_at":"2026-07-24T20:44:27Z","body":"I am not sure how this is relevant to the PR? Synchronising cycle phases is not something this addresses.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5074221942/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]